        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">Literature data\n\n# Included processes\nPlasticisers or water reducers, and superplasticiser or high range water reducers, are chemical admixtures that can be added to concrete mixtures to improve workability. Plasticisers are commonly manufactured from lignosulfonates, a by-product from the paper industry. Superplasticisers have generally been manufactured from sulfonated naphthalene condensate or sulfonated melamine formaldehyde, although newer products based on polycarboxylic ethers are now available.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
